@startuml server_connection_down
title Unreachable-Client Detection — Health Check & disconnect() Cleanup

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

note over ClientHandlerRmi, MatchManager
  This diagram covers what happens when the health-check thread on
  either transport decides a CLIENT is no longer reachable (it does
  not specifically detect a server-side network outage). Both paths
  converge on the same MatchManager.disconnect(nickname) method,
  which cleans up match/lobby/reconnection state and notifies any
  affected players. There is no special "server network down" branch:
  persistence of in-progress matches is kept current independently,
  via saveNow() after every successful move/draw/skip and via the
  JVM shutdown hook (see the disconnect() section below).
end note

== RMI — Health Check Detects Unreachable Client ==

participant "HealthCheck\nThread\n(inside CHR)" as HealthCheckRmi
participant "pingExecutor" as PE
participant "VirtualViewRmi\n(stub)" as STUB
participant "ClientHandlerRmi\n(CHR)" as CHR
participant "ServerRmi\n(DisconnectionListener)" as DL

note over HealthCheckRmi
  The HealthCheck thread runs INSIDE
  ClientHandlerRmi — it is not a
  separate object. Shown separately
  only for readability.
end note

HealthCheckRmi -> PE : pingExecutor.submit(\n  () -> clientStub.ping())

PE -> STUB : ping()  [remote call]
note right of STUB
  Server network is down:
  RMI blocks until PING_TIMEOUT (3000 ms)
end note

STUB --> PE : (hangs — no response)
PE --> HealthCheckRmi : future.get(PING_TIMEOUT) → TimeoutException

HealthCheckRmi -> HealthCheckRmi : ping.cancel(true)\nfailures++
note right : repeated up to MAX_FAILURES = 2\n(~6 s total before triggering)

note over HealthCheckRmi, CHR
  failures >= MAX_FAILURES:
  tryMarkDisconnected() is called directly
  by the HealthCheck thread (same object as CHR).
  Returns true → proceeds to notify listener.
end note

HealthCheckRmi -> CHR : tryMarkDisconnected()


HealthCheckRmi -> DL : disconnectionListener\n  .handleDisconnection(nickname)
note right of DL
  ServerRmi.handleDisconnection(nickname)
    → matchManager.disconnect(nickname)
end note

== Socket — Health Check Detects Unreachable Client ==

participant "HealthCheck\nThread\n(inside CHS)" as HealthCheckSck
participant "ClientHandlerSocket\n(CHS)" as CHS
participant "MatchManager" as MMsck

note over HealthCheckSck
  The HealthCheck thread runs INSIDE
  ClientHandlerSocket — not a separate object.
end note

note over HealthCheckSck, CHS
  Every PING_INTERVAL (2000 ms), a PingMessage is sent via sendAsync.
  lastMessageReceivedTime is updated on ANY incoming message (not just Pong).
  After TIMEOUT_LIMIT (6000 ms) of total inactivity (no message of any kind):
end note

HealthCheckSck -> HealthCheckSck : inactivity =\n  now - lastMessageReceivedTime\n  > TIMEOUT_LIMIT (6000 ms)

HealthCheckSck -> CHS : handleDisconnection(nickname)


CHS -> MMsck : matchManager.disconnect(nickname)

== MatchManager.disconnect() — Actual Cleanup Logic ==

participant "ServerRmi / CHS\n(caller)" as CALLER
participant "MatchManager" as MM
participant "ClientHandler\n[other players]" as CH_others3
participant "PersistenceManager" as PM

CALLER -> MM : disconnect(nickname)

note over MM
  Method body synchronizes on `this` —
  only one disconnect is processed at a
  time across all threads. disconnect()
  mirrors the four-branch logic of
  MatchManager.quit(), but never throws and
  always removes the client from `clients`
  at the end.

end note

alt active match (clientToMatch has nickname, not in a lobby, controller exists)
    MM -> MM : terminateMatch(matchId, nickname, reason)
    note right of MM
      terminateMatch():
      - removes ALL players of matchId from clientToMatch
      - controllers.remove(matchId) / gameManagers.remove(matchId)
      - persistenceManager.unregister(matchId)
        → deletes the match's save file (GameStateDAO.delete)
    end note
    MM -> CH_others3 : onQuitServer(reason)  [broadcast, disconnected player excluded]

else pending reconnection (clientToMatch has nickname, controller NOT yet rebuilt)
    MM -> MM : clientToMatch.remove(nickname)\nreconnectedPlayers[matchId].remove(nickname)\npendingRestorations.remove(matchId)\nreconnectedPlayers.remove(matchId)\npersistenceManager.unregister(matchId)
    MM -> CH_others3 : onQuitServer(reason)  [other players already reconnected, excluded the one disconnecting]

else in lobby (clientToMatch has nickname, lobby still open)
    MM -> MM : remove all lobby members from clientToMatch\nlobbies.remove(matchId)
    MM -> CH_others3 : onQuitServer(reason)  [other lobby members, excluded the one disconnecting]

else not tracked anywhere (e.g. pre-login or post-game)
    note right of MM
      No match/lobby/reconnection state for this
      nickname → reason stays null, nobody is notified.
      Unlike quit(), this branch does NOT throw
      InvalidTimingException: an untracked nickname
      is simply a silent no-op.
    end note
end

MM -> MM : clients.remove(nickname)

note over MM, PM
  Persistence safety net (unrelated to disconnect()):
  - MatchManager.move()/drawCard()/skip() each call
    persistenceManager.saveNow(matchId, gm) right after
    a successful action, so the on-disk snapshot is never
    more than one action stale.
  - The shutdown hook registered in MatchManager's
    constructor calls persistenceManager.shutdown(),
    which saveNow()s every still-active match when the
    JVM itself terminates.
end note

== On Server Restart ==

participant "MatchManager\n(new instance)" as MM2
participant "GameStateDAO" as DAO

MM2 -> DAO : GameStateDAO.loadAll()
note right of DAO
  Reads all match_*.json files from saves/
  Skips corrupted files (logged, not thrown)
end note
DAO --> MM2 : List<GameSnapshot>
MM2 -> MM2 : pendingRestorations.put(matchId, snap)\nreconnectedPlayers.put(matchId, {})\nnextMatchId advanced past saved IDs
note right of MM2
  Match waits in pendingRestorations.
  clientToMatch is NOT populated yet.
  As each player reconnects via login():
    → reconnectedPlayers[matchId].put(nickname, client)
    → clientToMatch.put(nickname, matchId)
    → client.onReconnection(matchId)
  When reconnectedPlayers[matchId].size()
    == snap.getNumPlayers()
  → restoreGame(matchId, snap) is called.
end note

@enduml
